  "notes": "Compound verb from {閉|と}じる (to close) + こもる (to seclude oneself). Intransitive.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {部屋|へや}に{閉|と}じこもる (to shut oneself in one's room)\n- {家|いえ}に{閉|と}じこもる (to stay shut up at home)\n- {殻|から}に{閉|と}じこもる (to withdraw into one's shell — figurative)\n\nUSAGE:\nCan range from neutral (staying home on a bad-weather day) to serious (social withdrawal associated with {引|ひ}きこもり). Context determines the tone. The figurative use {殻|から}に{閉|と}じこもる describes emotional withdrawal.",
